> score (indeed, some implementations might not even pretend that ascension
> scores are on the same numerical scale, but ascension > not-ascension is
> the thing that really matters.)

UnNetHack has changed the scoring mechanism such that you get
decreasing score for kills of the same species. Experience is
untouched.

The first kill gets you full points, the second half points, the nth
kill gets you 1/n points or at least 1 point.

This leads of course to smaller scores than in Vanilla. In the early
and middle games scores tend to be about half as high as in Vanilla.

Scores before ascension are between 1/2 and 2 million points.

This means that with ascensions you get the doubling of your score
*and* that items contribute again a larger part of the score.

It's still possible that non-ascensions get higher scores than
ascensions but this is by far not as easy as in Vanilla.

